      "writtenOn": "2024-06-21T09:00:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think you should modify the state in a function named `needs_thread`. When I read the code that calls `needs_thread`, I don\u0027t expect a state change. Also, if someone reorders or adds the condition to the if statement that calls needs_thread requested_thread_count could get incremented without sending a request to user-space. Technically even the C driver is not ideal here because it also increments requested_threads before call put_user (which could fail)",
      "revId": "5ca8d53de74dbdfccb391e64d62cc22d7ad24649",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
