        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-21T09:00:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is this for? We always put a noop placeholder at the start of the buffer. If this call is interrupted, it is still there when resumed, but your `has_noop_placeholder` is false at that point. I\u0027m not sure we ever get here with read_consumed !\u003d 0 though. The C driver does not update read_consumed when returning -EINTR (with only a noop in the buffer), so read_consumed will still be 0 when the ioctl is resumed. If any of the later CLs add a -EINTR return path where read_consumed !\u003d 0, then this variable can trigger a failure to request a new thread when a new thread is needed.",
      "revId": "5ca8d53de74dbdfccb391e64d62cc22d7ad24649",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
